(3171, 'Lalit ', 37, 'C++', 'What are access modifiers? ', 'Public,Private,Protected', 'You use access modifiers to define accessibility for the class members. It defines how to access the members of the class outside the class scope.', 1, 2, 2616),
(3172, 'Lalit ', 37, 'C++', 'Difference between equal to (==) and assignment operator(=)?', '== is boolean', ' The equal to operator == checks whether two values are equal or not. If equal, then it’s true; otherwise, it will return false.', 1, 2, 2616),
(3173, 'Lalit ', 37, 'C++', 'Can you compile a program without the main function? ', 'yes', 'Yes, you can compile a program without the main function, but you cannot run or execute the program because the main() function is the entry point, from where all the execution begins. And without the entry point, then you can execute the program.', 1, 2, 2616),
(3174, 'Lalit ', 37, 'C++', 'When is void() return type used?', 'when nothing to be returned', 'You use the void() return type when you don’t want to return any value. It specifies that the function doesn’t return a value.', 1, 2, 2616),
